.TH QT6DIALOG 1 "June 2026" "qt6sermo 1.0.0" "haplo-dialog User Commands"
.SH NAME
qt6sermo \- Qt6 dialog box creator for shell scripts
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B qt6sermo
[\fIOPTION\fR]...
.br
.B qt6sermo
\fB\-\-program\fR=\fIVARIABLE\fR
.br
.B qt6sermo
\fB\-\-file\fR=\fIFILE\fR
.br
.B qt6sermo
\fB\-\-stdin\fR
.br
.IR VARIABLE =\(aq<window>...</window>\(aq
.B qt6sermo
\fB\-\-program\fR=\fIVARIABLE\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B qt6sermo
reads a Qt6 GUI description written in an XML dialect and displays
the resulting dialog window.
It is designed to be called from shell scripts to present interactive forms,
progress bars, list views, and other widgets without requiring knowledge of
Qt6 programming.
.PP
The GUI description can be supplied from an environment variable
.RB ( \-\-program ),
a file
.RB ( \-\-file ),
or standard input
.RB ( \-\-stdin ).
.PP
When the dialog exits (for example when an action triggers EXIT),
.B qt6sermo
writes the current value of each named widget to standard output in the form:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
WIDGET_NAME="current_value"
.fi
.RE
.PP
which is typically captured with
.BR "eval $(qt6sermo ...)" .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-program= VARIABLE
Read the XML dialog description from the environment variable
.IR VARIABLE .
.TP
.BI \-\-file= FILE
Read the XML dialog description from
.IR FILE .
.TP
.B \-\-stdin
Read the XML dialog description from standard input.
.TP
.BI \-\-include= FILE
Include and execute
.I FILE
before running the main GUI description (shell functions).
.TP
.BI \-\-event\-driven= FILE
Execute
.I FILE
as an event-driven program.
.TP
.B \-\-print\-ir
Parse the GUI description, print the internal representation, and exit
without displaying any window.
.TP
.B \-\-debug
Enable debug mode (lexer character trace).
.TP
.BI \-\-geometry= GEOMETRY
Set the initial window placement and size (X11 convention).
.TP
.B \-\-center
Centre the windows on the screen.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-warning
Suppress non-fatal warning messages.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print version and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Print usage summary and exit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
The GUI description is read from the environment variable named by
.BR \-\-program .
Widget values are printed to standard output as
.B NAME="value"
assignments when the dialog exits.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/share/doc/qt6sermo/
Documentation, examples, and reference pages.
.TP
.I /usr/share/man/man1/qt6sermo.1.gz
This manual page.
.SH EXAMPLES
.SS Simple yes/no dialog
.nf
export DIALOG='
<window title="Confirm">
  <vbox>
    <text><label>Proceed?</label></text>
    <hbox>
      <button ok></button>
      <button cancel></button>
    </hbox>
  </vbox>
</window>'
qt6sermo --program=DIALOG
.fi
.SS Read entry value
.nf
export DIALOG='
<window>
  <vbox>
    <entry><variable>NAME</variable></entry>
    <button ok></button>
  </vbox>
</window>'
eval $(qt6sermo --program=DIALOG)
echo "Name: $NAME"
.fi
